      "note": [
        "A statistical method is used to protect the data of individuals in the statistics presented. For this reason, the presented totals do not always equal the sum of their reported components. See also section 2.2.6 Model assumptions in the quality declaration documentation on Statistics Sweden’s website.",
        "The statistics are intended to describe the location of the workplaces with which the employed people are associated. Since this is not the same as presenting the employed part of the population by their physical location during the daytime when work is performed, the term “daytime population” is not used. Consequently, the term 'night-time population' is not used either in the reporting according to region of residence.",
        "The statistics are by month. Quarterly and annual data is calculated as the average of the months included.",
        "As of 2023, the retirement age was raised from 65 to 66 years, and as of 2026, to 67 years. For this reason, statistics are reported for age groups up to 64, 65, and 66 years.",
        "2026-05-28: The preliminary statistics from January 2020 to February 2026 have been revised. More information in Swedish can be found in [Revidering av preliminär statistik från Befolkningens arbetsmarknadsstatus](https://www.scb.se/contentassets/f7fc10dacfef4075a98be3b56724f7e6/revidering-i-preliminar-bas-statistik.pdf)"
